; bfsodium INVSUBBYTES : every byte of the state through the INVERSE S box
;
; NOTE square brackets are brainfuck loops  so comments use braces for counts;
;
; HAND WRITTEN; block/invsbox256 block/walk256 and block/rotate16 are
; INCLUDED;
;
; IO  in:  state{16}   (16 bytes)
;     out: state{16}   every byte replaced by its inverse S box entry
;
; FIPS 197 section 5 point 3 point 2; The inverse S box is block/sbox256
; read backwards  which cannot disagree with the permutation it came from;
; This file is aes/subbytes with the other table: same walk  same conveyor
; same layout  and the same cost for the same data  with only the 256
; constants differing;
;
; THERE IS NO INTERFACE LINE AND THAT IS FORCED; the walk advances three cells
; a turn  so no loop in it is pointer balanced  so tools/bffoot cannot bound a
; footprint and tools/bfexpand will not paste this; An INCLUDE does not care
; and that is why the walk is a block;
;
; ONE WALK  WRITTEN ONCE  RUN SIXTEEN TIMES; the earlier cut of this file
; unrolled sixteen walks and ran to 750 skeleton lines  which is past the size
; at which a person writes a file rather than generates one; The state is
; TURNED instead: block/rotate16 brings a different byte under the fixed read
; point each turn  and sixteen turns put the run back as it was;
;
; THE CONVEYOR IS AFFORDABLE AND THE WALK IS NOT; on FIPS 197 Appendix B's
; round one state the sixteen walks cost 4 million 750 thousand instructions
; and the machinery that lets one walk serve for all sixteen costs 324
; thousand against that: six point eight percent; That 324 thousand is
; block/rotate16 at 12 thousand 314 a turn plus the two seventeen cell byte
; moves that feed the walk;
;
; THE FILE AS A WHOLE IS ONLY SIX POINT FOUR PERCENT DEARER  because this cut
; also swapped a PACKED ABSOLUTE table for block/sbox256's delta coded one:
; 34 thousand 193 instructions down to 17 thousand 149; So the net against
; the unrolled file is 307 thousand while the loop machinery alone is 324
; thousand  and quoting the net as the cost of the turning would credit the
; conveyor with a saving that belongs to the table;
;
; THAT SHARE IS NOT A CONSTANT; a turn's cost tracks the byte values it
; carries and a walk's tracks the index it walks to  so the share runs from
; four point one percent on a state of 0xff to worse than double on a state
; of nought  where every walk stops at the first group; It is quoted at a
; published state because real states are not nought;
;
; One turn of the 256 cell TABLE would cost about as much as a whole walk
; which is why the table is walked and only the state is turned; HANDOFF
; carries both measurements;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000        cnt    u8  bytes still to do  starts at sixteen
;   @0x001        t      u8  the cell block/rotate16 turns the run through
;   @0x002:0x011  state{16}  read here  and the answers come back here
;   @0x012:0x014  group 0 of the walk; ITS TRAIL IS NEVER SET  which is what
;                 stops the walk back; the index goes into its walker at
;                 @0x013 and the answer comes to rest there
;   @0x015:0x314  groups 1 to 256  the INVERSE S box; element k in group k
;                 plus one  with its datum at 21 plus 3k

  >>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,>,                            ; the state  and nothing else: the table is a constant
                                                               ; and is written below
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=17
                                                               ; ASSERT zero 18:788
>>>>                                                           ; to the first datum of the table
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=21
                                                               ; invS the inverse AES S box  two hundred and fifty six
                                                               ; entries  one to a line laid out for the stride three
                                                               ; walk: datum  walker  trail  so each entry is followed
                                                               ; by a step of three; the caller walks in to the first
                                                               ; datum and back out from the last;
;
                                                               ; FIPS 197 section 5 point 3 point 2; DERIVED and not
                                                               ; typed  and the form is the one sha256/hashcore uses
                                                               ; for its round constants: a comment naming the value
                                                               ; then a delta coded run  shorter direction  which
                                                               ; leans on the cell wrapping at 256 and halves the
                                                               ; cost;
;
                                                               ; It is block/sbox256 read backwards: invS at S of i is
                                                               ; i; A permutation read backwards cannot disagree with
                                                               ; the permutation it came from; invS of 0x00 is 0x52
  ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
